In article <12270@orstcs.CS.ORST.EDU> kstclair@jacobs.CS.ORST.EDU.UUCP (Kelly St.Clair) writes:

>For new players and inexperienced players, however, the game is nigh
>unbeatable.  Monsters are tougher, hit harder, and don't leave edible
>corpses very often.  New features (like not being able to #sacrifice
>except at altars) make some of the old tricks harder to put into 
>practice.  Players who were used to striding confidently through the
>Dungeon are now lucky to make it down to Dlevel 3 without starving or
>being killed by one hit from a monster they used to feel only moderately
>nervous about.  For these players, the game is not fun, or even a challenge,
>only frustrating.

Do I hear a call for difficulty levels in NetHack 4.0?  Could be interesting,
but a little tough to implement.

For my self: I used to play Hack and cheat by copying save files.  Then I 
stopped playing.  Then I got Nethack 2.3 and decided not to cheat any more.
Rarely did I get below Dlevel 10 and only once did I get down far enough to
be killed by Medusa.  Never laid eyes on Amulet nor Wizard.  But I still
liked the game.

NH3 however, is tough!  I guess we need a new nethack tutorial.  Once I had
a good character going, 5th level, 60 HP, good armor, +2 Longsword.  I stepped
into a room and got the message "You feel hemmed in."  Suddenly I was
surrounded by about 10 "d"s, 5 "r"s and a couple of "q"s.  Hardly seemed
fair.  I got off one swing, was attacked about 15 times, one more swing and
you guessed it, I was jackal bait.  I want to know how the NetGods would have
handled that situation.  No magic on me at the time :-(

But still I play.  I don't know why.  I guess I'll never see the wizard.  Could
someone post complete instructions for playing in explore mode, i.e. how
to do it (What's the command line switch?) and any hot keys, or other helps?
If it's in the nethack help just point me there.  Thanks.

